            implicit split command to the @F array is done as the first thing
            inside the implicit while loop produced by the "-n" or "-p".

                perl -ane 'print pop(@F), "\n";'

            is equivalent to

                while (<>) {
                    @F = split(' ');
                    print pop(@F), "\n";
